---
source: tests/cli_snapshots.rs
expression: stdout
---
Check files for spelling errors

Usage: matchum check [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments:
  [PATHS]...  Files or directories to check [default: .]

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>            Config file path
  -f, --format <FORMAT>            Output format: text, json, github, words-only [default: text]
      --suggestions                Show spelling suggestions
      --unique                     Only show unique misspelled words
      --strict                     Exit with code 1 if any spelling errors found
  -t, --type <FILE_TYPE>           Only check files of this type (e.g., rust, python, js)
      --stats                      Show execution statistics
      --diff                       Read unified diff from stdin; only report issues on added lines
  -e, --exclude <EXCLUDE>          Exclude files matching the glob pattern (can be used multiple times)
      --locale <LOCALE>            Set language locales (e.g., "en,fr" or "en-GB")
      --language-id <LANGUAGE_ID>  Force programming language for unknown extensions
      --no-issues                  Do not show the spelling errors
      --no-progress                Turn off progress messages
      --no-summary                 Turn off summary message
      --quiet                      Only show spelling issues or errors
  -s, --silent                     Silent mode, suppress error messages
      --relative                   Use paths relative to the config file or root
      --fail-fast                  Exit after first file with an issue or error
      --dot                        Show hidden files
      --no-gitignore               Do not use .gitignore
      --root <ROOT>                Set the root directory for relative paths
      --file-list <FILE_LIST>      Specify a list of files to be spell checked
  -h, --help                       Print help
